From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 18:31:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: g16: Release a closed VM's compute leases
 once retired

A compute unit's last-owner lease now holds only the owner's compute
arena, but it is still released only when another VM's compute command
retires on the same unit. Up to sixteen closed VMs' arenas, about 40 MiB
each, can therefore stay mapped until reboot on a desktop that runs no
compute.

When a VM's handle is closed (after its last job guard, so none of its
commands is in flight), drop its compute leases on units that are fully
retired. A unit whose owner closes while its command is still in flight
drops the lease when that command passes the full receipt. Quarantined
units keep their lease.

The firmware's descriptor retire runs at each compute completion before
the notifier store that the full receipt waits for. It saves the
descriptor row and clears the binding, so a fully retired unit leaves
the firmware no reference into the owner's arena or address space.

The runtime parameter g16_lease_release (default 1) restores the old
behaviour when set to 0. The stats line counts the released leases.

Assisted-by: LLM
